<title>UK: BT's expansive global partnerships -- an overview.</title>
<headline>BT's expansive global partnerships -- an overview.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here follows a list of the world-wide deals struck by British Telecommunications Plc around the global after Spain's flagship carrier Telefonica de Espana SA said on Friday it was joining the expanding alliance.</p>
<p>THE ALLIANCE: BT and MCI Communications Corp, who together form the Concert global alliance, which plans to span the world, offering sophisticated communications services.</p>
<p>JOINT VENTURES:</p>
<p>Belize</p>
<p>Brazil (Proceda)</p>
<p>Canada (BT visual images)</p>
<p>France (Cegetel)</p>
<p>Germany (Viag Interkom)</p>
<p>Gibraltar</p>
<p>India (BHARTI Cellular, Mahindra-BT, Wipro-BT)</p>
<p>Italy (Albacom)</p>
<p>Japan (NIS, Telehouse, K-Net, Tu-ka mobile companies)</p>
<p>Korea (Dacom)</p>
<p>Mexico (Avantel)</p>
<p>Netherlands (Telfort)</p>
<p>New Zealand (Clear Communications)</p>
<p>Indonesia (PT INDOSAT, Panorama Timur Java)</p>
<p>Russia (SPI)</p>
<p>Saudi Arabia (AT al-Saudia Ltd)</p>
<p>Spain (Telefonica)</p>
<p>Sweden (Telenordia)</p>
<p>Switzerland (Newtelco).</p>
<p>DISTRIBUTORS OF CONCERT COMMUNICATIONS SERVICES:</p>
<p>Africa (Grinakr Telekom, Persetel Networks)</p>
<p>Austria (MDIS), Columbia (Rey Moreno)</p>
<p>Czech Republic (GTS)</p>
<p>Denmark (Tele Danmark A/S )</p>
<p>Greece (Space Hellas)</p>
<p>Hungary (GTS)</p>
<p>Israel (Tadiran Ltd )</p>
<p>Japan (Adamnet, Fusions SyNI+C, Mutsumi Tsishin, NRI, NTT Data)</p>
<p>Kenya (Comm Carrier)</p>
<p>Lebanon (Data Management, SAL)</p>
<p>Malaysia (Telekom Malaysia Bhd, Berhad, Sime Darby</p>
<p>Systems, O'Connors Engineering and Trading)</p>
<p>North East Asia (Unisys Corp ), Norway (Telenor)</p>
<p>Oman (GTO, Wacom)</p>
<p>Philippines (Philcom)</p>
<p>Poland (Telbank)</p>
<p>Portugal (Portugal Telecom SA)</p>
<p>Romania (Logic Telecom)</p>
<p>Russia (IAS)</p>
<p>Singapore (CSA Holdings Ltd, Singapore</p>
<p>Telecommunications Ltd )</p>
<p>Slovakia (Eurotel, Bratislava Ltd)</p>
<p>South Africa (FirstNet Telekom South)</p>
<p>Taiwan (Chung Hwa Development Ltd )</p>
<p>Thailand (CAT).</p>
<p>MEMBERSHIP OF SATELLITE CONSORTIA:</p>
<p>European Telecommuncations Satellite Organisation (EUTELSAT)</p>
<p>International Maritime Satellite Organisation (INMARSAT)</p>
<p>International Telecommunications Satellite Organisation</p>
<p>(INTELSAT)</p>
<p>OTHER GLOBAL PARTNERS:</p>
<p>Jetphone BT and France Cable Radio (FCR), Skyphone (BT, Telenor</p>
<p>International and Singapore Telecom)</p>
